WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.869
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.869 --> 00:00:09.160
In 1919 a young ambitious 30-year-old stood
in a beer hall in Munich, Germany and gave

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:14.000
a passionate speech about politics to 111
attendees.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.630
Only four months later, the same young man
gave another speech, but this time, due to

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:22.550
word of mouth, his audience had grown to over
2000.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:30.980
A few months later he gives another speech
with 6,000 devotees in attendance.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.390
This is how revolutions begin.

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:39.670
That ambitious young man went on to change
the world beyond recognition, by committing

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:45.039
countless atrocities against the human race
and attempting genocide.

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:48.470
Yes I am talking about Adolf Hitler.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:53.840
Do not take my words as praise, but there
is no doubt that Hitler’s oration abilities

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.490
are unrivalled throughout history.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:01:01.510
His ability to persuade others and bring them
into his cause and align their ideals with

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:04.830
his own were powerful beyond belief.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:12.230
During one 2 hour speech in 1920 he was completely
interrupted 58 times by thundering applause

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:14.280
and cheers from the crowd.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:19.870
But was Adolf Hitler a great leader?

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:24.770
Absolutely not, effective maybe, but great,
no.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:30.700
As humans with a conscience we define great
as doing good, therefore a great leader must

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:36.170
use their power and influence for good, not
evil as Hitler did.

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:41.620
But besides the obvious deplorable reasons
that Hitler was not a great leader, he wasn’t

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:45.280
actually good at leading.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:52.020
Let me explain, Hitler was a fantastic orator,
he gave speeches so powerful, so intense that

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.170
they made you forget your morals and follow
him into a genocidal abyss.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:01.750
He was extremely effective at collecting followers
and power.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:06.960
But being able to rally hearts and minds is
only one half of being a great leader.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:13.250
For, once Hitler had that power, he was hopeless
at putting it to use, at least when you compare

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.220
him to his wartime competition.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:20.820
A truly great leader in Hitler’s position
of immense power would have leveraged Germany’s

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:26.320
strengths and turned wartime Germany into
a true superpower, a force to be reckoned

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.320
with.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:32.110
And a true leader could of done so without
ever going to war, using only diplomacy and

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.110
leverage.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.110
There were many years leading up to the war
when a great leader could have turned Germany

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:35.110
into the modern world’s first superpower
giving Germany a far better chance of winning

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.110
the war or better yet, bypassing it altogether.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.630
But Hitler was too consumed by his own hate
and pride.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:43.410
His deep hatred of Jews, communists and others
caused him to get distracted by and drawn

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:49.980
into many futile conflicts that were completely
unnecessary and only hindered Germany’s

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.960
overall strength, such as Stalingrad.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.120
He was more concerned with destroying his
neighboroughing countries than focusing on

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:00.370
the strengths of his own, Germany.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:08.170
These are certainly not the traits of a great
leader, just a passionate, angry fool.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:12.370
Are you passionate about something, but tired
of feeling like a fool?

