00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:33.669
Hitler’s wartime enemy Winston Churchill
is also thought of as one of history’s most

00:04:33.669 --> 00:04:39.660
powerful leaders, but unlike Hitler, many
people go as far as to call Churchill a great

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.320
leader.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:42.730
So what’s the difference?

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:47.410
Is Churchill only a great leader, and Hitler
is not because Churchill was fighting for

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.410
good, not evil?

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:53.960
Well that certainly helps, but it’s the
reason why Churchill was fighting for good

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.470
which made him a truly great leader.

00:04:56.470 --> 00:05:01.620
And that reason is a great empathy for his
people.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:06.940
Hitler’s motivation for going to war was
occupation of neighbouring countries to expand

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:14.630
the German empire and his idea of a “pure
race” and also genocide, these are selfish

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:20.350
reasons, Hitler’s powerful oration may have
tricked millions into believing that he had

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:27.030
the German people’s best interests in mind,
but in truth his motivations were not only

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:32.880
selfish, but driven by delusions, insecurity
and mental insanity.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:38.919
Churchill’s motivations were the polar-opposite,
he went to war to defend his people and his

00:05:38.919 --> 00:05:44.990
country from the tyranny of evil, he had no
desire to invade and capture other lands or

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:48.180
to enslave and murder innocent people.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:53.480
Psychologists have long studied what it takes
to be a great leader and they have all converged

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:58.910
on one key quality that every great leader
from history shared.

00:05:58.910 --> 00:06:07.180
One mental attribute that separates Churchill
from Hitler, emotional intelligence.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:13.570
It is not intellect, cunning or physical prowess
that makes a great leader, it is emotional

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:14.570
intelligence.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:19.970
That is the ability to sympathise with others,
to know how people think, behave and how they

00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:22.690
will react given any situation.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.070
What made Abraham Lincoln such a great leader?

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.990
Such an icon, respected throughout the ages.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:33.830
How was he able to overcome the tremendous
challenges in abolishing slavery?

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:37.560
He possessed more emotional intelligence than
his enemies.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:41.840
Whilst the plantation owners and leaders of
the confederacy were only concerned with monetary

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.720
gain from their slaves.

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:48.260
Lincoln was able to sympathise with the plight
of the slaves, he could humanise them and

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:54.270
this gave him the drive, the passion, the
motivation to put every fibre of himself into

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:59.820
his quest to set them free, and that he did.

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:06.610
Hitler may have been an extremely intelligent
man, an incredible orator and powerfully persuasive,

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:13.509
but he had not a scrap of emotional intelligence,
he had no sympathy.

00:07:13.509 --> 00:07:17.060
No man who did the things he did could possess
these qualities.

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:24.370
But Churchill, despite his image as a pragmatic
bulldog, did and that’s why he led Britain

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:27.030
and the World to victory.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:31.550
But being a great leader isn’t just being
able to make the correct decision.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:37.680
A truly great leader must also be able to
make the hardest decision of all, when it

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.490
is most needed of them.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:41.880
No matter the cost.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:46.509
On 10th May 1940 Winston Churchill was appointed
Prime Minister of Great Britain.

00:07:46.509 --> 00:07:51.300
On the very same day, Hitler launched a huge
invasion of France.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.280
occupying vast swathes of the country.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.700
Before long Hitler’s army had occupied Paris
and forced the nation of France to surrender.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:03.550
When Churchill heard that France was prepared
to surrender and make a peace deal with Hitler

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:08.479
he knew that if the Nazis were to get their
hands on France’s navy, which at the time

00:08:08.479 --> 00:08:13.910
was the second most powerful in the world,
after Britain’s, then Britain would be screwed.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:19.740
Sure, Britain’s navy was powerful, but with
the combined might of France’s Navy and

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:25.910
Germany’s U-boats, Britain would have been
Hitler’s for the taking, and worse yet,

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:31.919
if Hitler took Britain, and its navy, the
rest of the world would have stood no chance

00:08:31.919 --> 00:08:34.189
against the spread of Hitler’s tyranny.

00:08:34.189 --> 00:08:40.189
with all that combined military might, he
could have taken the US with ease and today

00:08:40.189 --> 00:08:46.990
the world would be under Nazi rule, simply
because Hitler got his hands on a few French

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:47.990
warships.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:51.129
Churchill could absolutely not let this happen.

00:08:51.129 --> 00:08:56.410
Initially he wrote to the US president FDR
and asked if he could borrow fifty of their

00:08:56.410 --> 00:09:01.860
older warships to defend Britain in the event
that Hitler took France’s navy, but FDR

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:08.110
was too concerned with winning the upcoming
election and so denied Churchill’s request,

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:13.009
even after Churchill wrote back to him explaining
that if Britain was taken then America would

00:09:13.009 --> 00:09:14.040
be next.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:19.560
The French Admiral had made a promise to Churchill
that if the Nazis did ever try to take France’s

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:24.999
warships then the French would sabotage their
own ships rendering them useless to Hitler.

00:09:24.999 --> 00:09:32.190
But Churchill was too pragmatic to rely solely
on the French disabling their own ships and

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:36.760
so he formulated a grand plan called operation
Catapult.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:42.629
The most daring and most morally difficult
plan that Churchill had so far enacted.

00:09:42.629 --> 00:09:48.209
France’s vast navy was spread out in fleets
around the globe, so Churchill planned to

00:09:48.209 --> 00:09:55.390
use espionage, stealth and if necessary force
to capture all of France’s warships and

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.749
relocate them to British waters.

00:09:57.749 --> 00:10:04.769
So, on the 3rd July 1940 operation Catapult
was launched and simultaneous takeovers of

00:10:04.769 --> 00:10:09.130
every French naval vessel took place within
a few hours around the globe.

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:14.300
Bearing in mind that until now, France was
Britain’s closest ally during the war, this

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:20.220
must have been a horrendously difficult decision
for Churchill to make, but the decision that

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:26.860
he had to make in just a few hour’s time
would be many times more difficult, in fact

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:32.230
it would arguably be the most difficult, the
most heart-wrenching decision the Prime Minister

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.470
would make his entire life.

00:10:34.470 --> 00:10:39.649
A decision that many historians have since
said was one of the biggest turning points

00:10:39.649 --> 00:10:43.389
of the war and changed the fate of the World.

00:10:43.389 --> 00:10:49.160
You see, all but one of the fleets within
the French navy could be taken with little

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:54.569
effort by simply sneaking British servicemen
onboard and putting a gun up to the captain.

00:10:54.569 --> 00:11:00.910
But one fleet, the strongest and most heavily
guarded within France’s navy would not be

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:02.249
so simple.

00:11:02.249 --> 00:11:07.730
In the harbour of Mers-el-Kébir in French
Algeria, France had moored their four largest

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:14.439
and most powerful ships, the Bretagne, Provence,
Strasbourg and Dunkerque, as well as some

00:11:14.439 --> 00:11:16.399
smaller destroyers.

00:11:16.399 --> 00:11:21.269
If Hitler got his hands on just this fleet
alone it would spell the end of the war for

00:11:21.269 --> 00:11:23.060
Britain and the world.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:28.300
Churchill wrote an ultimatum to the French
admiral and sent out a fleet of the Royal

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:33.389
Navy’s most powerful vessels to deliver
it to the French fleet at Mers-el-Kebir.

00:11:33.389 --> 00:11:39.739
It gave France just six hours from receiving
the letter to sail their large fleet of warships

00:11:39.739 --> 00:11:48.189
to Britain or America and surrender them or
the British Navy will regrettably sink them

00:11:48.189 --> 00:11:49.360
using force.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:54.279
The Royal Navy surrounded the French fleet
and a long, intense standoff wore on for many

00:11:54.279 --> 00:12:00.829
hours as the French Admiral refused to peacefully
surrender his ships to the British, their

00:12:00.829 --> 00:12:01.829
allies.

00:12:01.829 --> 00:12:06.320
The French admiral was annoyed that Churchill
obviously didn’t trust his promise that

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:11.499
the French navy would destroy their own ships
if the Nazis tried to take them, he was also

00:12:11.499 --> 00:12:15.459
annoyed that a lower ranking member of the
Royal Navy was sent to deliver Churchill’s

00:12:15.459 --> 00:12:19.339
ultimatum to him, instead of someone higher
up in the command.

00:12:19.339 --> 00:12:24.850
He also didn’t believe that the British
would actually fire upon them if they refused

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:26.839
to hand over their ships.

00:12:26.839 --> 00:12:32.149
So with the French Admiral remaining stubborn
the two supposedly allied nations, stood gun

00:12:32.149 --> 00:12:35.870
to gun across the harbour in a Mexican standoff.

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:40.459
A few hours later the French Admiral called
on nearby backup just in case the British

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:42.199
did decide to open fire.

00:12:42.199 --> 00:12:47.459
But the British soon caught wind of the encroaching
backup and so the captain sent a telegram

00:12:47.459 --> 00:12:48.459
to Number 10.

00:12:48.459 --> 00:12:52.040
Informing Churchill of the incoming French
backup only minutes away.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:57.819
Churchill was suddenly weighed down by his
worst fear, that it would have to come to

00:12:57.819 --> 00:13:03.610
this, the possibility of ordering the British
to shoot upon their own allies.

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:09.799
With little time to think he sent back a short,
sharp reply “Settle matters quickly.”

00:13:09.799 --> 00:13:14.809
and that was it, knowing full well what that
might entail.

00:13:14.809 --> 00:13:19.230
Regrettably the British fleet knew what they
had to do next, as Churchill had briefed them

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:20.230
beforehand.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:25.820
Yet the British signalled the French ship
once more, giving them one last warning, come

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:29.949
to an agreement within 30 minutes or we will
open fire.

00:13:29.949 --> 00:13:37.929
At 5:54pm no agreement had been reached and
sure enough the British pointed their cannons

00:13:37.929 --> 00:13:41.119
at the French vessels and began to fire.

00:13:41.119 --> 00:13:47.709
The British fleet that day consisted of battleships
HMS Valiant and HMS Resolution, an aircraft

00:13:47.709 --> 00:13:50.019
carrier and several destroyers.

00:13:50.019 --> 00:13:55.869
But at the helm of the fleet was the Royal
Navy’s most powerful weapon, HMS Hood, the

00:13:55.869 --> 00:14:01.829
largest and most powerful warship in the world
at that time, completely unmatched by any

00:14:01.829 --> 00:14:02.829
other ship.

00:14:02.829 --> 00:14:09.249
Her huge turrets fired relentlessly upon the
French battleships, sinking one and completely

00:14:09.249 --> 00:14:13.430
destroying the others within minutes.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:21.230
1,297 French servicemen lost their lives that
day at the hand of the British, supposedly

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:22.879
their closest ally.

00:14:22.879 --> 00:14:27.959
Whilst the British public and government were
entirely supportive of Churchill’s decision

00:14:27.959 --> 00:14:33.399
when they found out what had happened, many
others around the world, particularly the

00:14:33.399 --> 00:14:39.009
French were both critical and upset at Britain’s
actions that day, seeing on betrayal.

00:14:39.009 --> 00:14:44.509
It could be argued that Churchill’s move
to sink the French navy was over the top and

00:14:44.509 --> 00:14:52.620
rash but one has to consider what the other
outcome would have been, if Hitler had got

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:59.199
his hands on those French battleships, it
is entirely possible that the entire world,

00:14:59.199 --> 00:15:03.119
not just Britain, would be under Nazi rule
today.

00:15:03.119 --> 00:15:07.299
It is reported that when word got back to
Churchill in London about what had happened

00:15:07.299 --> 00:15:14.220
in Mers-el-Kébir and how many French servicemen
had been killed he was physically sick and

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.300
broke down in tears.

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:21.829
Whether you agree with operation catapult
or not no one can argue how incomprehensibly

00:15:21.829 --> 00:15:27.889
difficult a decision of that magnitude must
have been for Churchill or any other leader

00:15:27.889 --> 00:15:29.470
to make.

00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:36.299
Churchill sacrificed over a thousand of Britain’s
allies that day to save the British people

00:15:36.299 --> 00:15:42.889
and potentially the world from the tyranny
of evil, a horrible decision to make with

00:15:42.889 --> 00:15:48.621
irreparable consequences, but if that’s
not true leadership then I don’t know what

00:15:48.621 --> 00:15:49.819
is.

00:15:49.819 --> 00:15:54.779
Winston Churchill was recently voted by the
British public as the greatest Briton of all

00:15:54.779 --> 00:16:00.279
time and sure it’s tremendously easy to
see how he is great leader.

00:16:00.279 --> 00:16:05.439
He stared pure evil in the face when the rest
of his cabinet wanted to surrender, he led

00:16:05.439 --> 00:16:08.889
Britain and Western Europe through its darkest
hour.

00:16:08.889 --> 00:16:14.429
He was a master of the english language and
used it to inspire and uplift the moral of

00:16:14.429 --> 00:16:15.619
the British people.

00:16:15.619 --> 00:16:20.929
But how come there are some leaders today
that are considered by their people as great,

00:16:20.929 --> 00:16:24.290
when the rest of the world can only see the
opposite?

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:29.739
It used to be that good and evil was so black
and white, you would look at the world stage

00:16:29.739 --> 00:16:34.959
and the vast differences between the goodies
and the baddies was laid out bare for all

00:16:34.959 --> 00:16:35.959
to see.

00:16:35.959 --> 00:16:42.089
But today our leaders are becoming ever more
grey, treading a thin line between good and

00:16:42.089 --> 00:16:43.319
evil.

00:16:43.319 --> 00:16:49.410
Leaders such as Donald Trump and Kim Jong
Un are so polarising yet so murky.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:55.480
Sure leaders have always had supporters and
detractors but in today’s information driven

00:16:55.480 --> 00:17:01.980
world it’s so easy to find out why supposedly
bad leaders do the things they do, instead

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.500
of relying on propaganda.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:11.060
And with nobody is the balance between good
and evil more murkier, harder to understand

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:13.700
than with Vladimir Putin.

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:24.079
You cannot talk about great leaders without
including Putin, for nobody is more loved

00:17:24.079 --> 00:17:25.600
by their own people.

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:32.640
Okay, maybe Kim Jong Un is, but under entirely
different circumstances.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:38.440
Every single week an army of polsters traverses
the 11 different time zones of Russia and

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:43.790
knocks on the doors of every single house
in the country, asking their opinion of Vladimir

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.200
Putin and other political issues.

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:50.830
According to these polls Vladimir Putin’s
approval rating by his own people is a staggering

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:56.450
83% and has not dropped below 80% since 2014.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:18:02.290
And these numbers aren’t superficially increased
by the Kremlin, several independent Western

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:08.700
polling companies have done similar polls
and always arrive around the same number.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:15.170
To put that into perspective Trump’s approval
rating is half of that at 40%, Theresa May’s

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:21.770
is 43% and Angela Merkel’s is around 50%,
at the time of writing this video.

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:23.860
But how can this be?

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:29.840
Doesn’t most of the west view Putin as a
bad guy? Or a troublemaker at the very least.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:36.260
And it’s easy to see why, Putin has done
some rather questionable and immoral things

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:42.450
including annexing Crimea, waging a war on
the LGBT community, he is suspected of having

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:47.640
critics and political enemies killed and the
most questionable act of all, he is of course

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:52.270
rumored to have used hacking campaigns and
propaganda to make Trump president.

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:58.290
But no matter how much western politicians
and western media demonises him, his approval

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:02.910
rating within Motherland Russia just keep
increasing with time.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:08.790
To appreciate why we have to understand the
vast difference in culture between Russia

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.680
and the West.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:17.530
Russians respect strength, whilst Western
Europeans may have ideals such as fair democracy,

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:24.490
social equality and justice, it is ingrained
within the Russian culture to never show weakness.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:29.480
Russians strive for the solidification and
strengthening of their own nation.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:34.010
They have a great respect for Russia and any
president who can make Russia appear to be

00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:40.370
strong and not a pushover on the world stage
is no doubt going to be popular.

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:46.840
Putin does exactly that, the propaganda released
from the Kremlin is carefully curated to always

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:52.520
show Putin in positions of strength and in
manly pursuits like fishing topless, hunting

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:58.820
topless and riding a shark, I mean horse,
topless!

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:02.010
There seems to be a theme here.

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:07.150
These are not candid holiday snaps, these
are carefully curated to show Putin in his

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:09.420
best and strongest light.

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:13.910
He appears formidable and able to take on
whatever the West throws at him.

00:20:13.910 --> 00:20:19.580
Putin may not play nicely on the global stage
but whether you sympathise with Putin’s

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:27.020
methods of politics or not he is in his own
way and for the Russian people at least, a

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:28.350
great leader.

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:34.039
Leaders come in many forms, throughout history
some have led us into the dark abyss, other

00:20:34.039 --> 00:20:39.150
have led us to victory but one thing that
all great leaders do is bring about change

00:20:39.150 --> 00:20:44.830
within the world and leave their own unique
footprint on the future, sometime for the

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:47.610
best, sometimes for the worst.

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:53.280
So wherever you are in the world, when the
time next comes for you to choose a leader,

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:59.670
make your choice worthwhile.

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:09.400
Thanks for watching.

